[Music]  it was a strong year for new releases  but a number of expansions for existing  games wowed us as well an expansion to  The Witcher 3 Wild Hunt appears on our  list for a second straight year as CD  Projekt RED followed up last year's  excellent hearts of stone expansion with  another hit blood and wine debuting in  May the add-on transported players to  the vibrant and colorful world of  Toussaint's quests and activities  abounded while new features like a  mutation system gave players the ability  to add passive bonuses and other skill  facts this was a welcome feature as it  added a new flavor to combat and the way  you can interact with the world with The  Witcher 3 being the final Witcher game  to star garel and this being its last  expansion the monster hunter goes out in  style with blood and wine in the PC  space blizzards genre-defining MMO World  of Warcraft welcomed its six expansion  in August Legion was praised by GameSpot  and others for its story that had  genuine stakes and consequences while  the new demon hunter class shakes things  up by being more action-oriented than  others the new zones are some of the  most expansive and diverse ever seen in  the game overall Blizzard proves all  over again with Legion that it knows how  to bring players back with an epic  expansion dying light the following  landed in February evolving the game's  core formula with new mechanics and  features and the standout one being the  dirt buggy running around on foot is  fine but being able to cover more ground  in a car dials up the moment-to-moment  excitement significantly whereas the  base game is focused on parkour ready  environments the following takes place  upside of her on to a new vehicle  friendly world as you progress through  the DLC you pick up new upgrades for  your buggy including the likes of  flamethrowers and deployable mines the  expansion overall is a beefy one  including a main story side missions and  even new skill based challenges we won't  spoil it here but the ending had a  pretty cool story twist and we did  coming blizzards hearthstone heroes of  Warcraft had one of the best add-ons in  2016 in whispers of the old gods  released in May whispers of the old gods  mixed things up with a hundred and  thirty-four new cards including those  for the famous Warcraft characters  C'thun ye'arj yogg-saron and nazar the  expansion also changed up the popular  collectible card games formula with a  new standard and wild mode in standard  mode you can play with a deck that pulls  from a pool of cards released in the  current and previous calendar year wild  mode on the other hand is a format where  anything can happen this expansion felt  fresh with new features and took steps  to make the free-to-play game more  accessible for newcomers another shining  example of expansion content this year  came in the form of strategy game XCOM  two's Shen's last gift add on the  expansion lets you bring sentient robots  called sparks in the battle the Robo  creatures have more health and firepower  than a standard human soldier and  because they can't take cover you'll  need to adjust your strategy like human  characters the sparks also have to  progression paths to move through giving  you a reason to stick with the  characters over the long haul there's  also an excellent news story mission to  take on where you play as engineer Lily  Shen Shen's last gift is a present  you'll be happy to open  [Music]

